gfx803 (Polaris, GCN3): wire the ISA family up so triton's AMD backend does
not hard-reject the target.

WHY
---
Triton's AMD backend rejects any arch whose ISA family is Unknown
(TritonGPUToLLVM.cpp, ConvertWarpPipeline.cpp). gfx803 is pre-RDNA/pre-CDNA
GCN, so `TargetFeatures::getISAFamily()` fell through every branch and
returned Unknown. Verified on real RX 470 hardware (2026-08-21): with this
patch, an add kernel and tl.dot GEMMs (3 shapes) compile, load and run with
exact results (maxerr=0.0000). See patches/triton/README.md for the full
verification record.

RE-DIFF (2026-09-07)
---------------------
Re-diffed against triton-lang/triton @ 675c59878 (the exact commit
ROCm/pytorch release/2.14 pins triton to). The original 2026-08-21 patch
targeted third_party/amd/{include,lib}/TritonAMDGPUToLLVM/TargetUtils.{h,cpp},
a free-function `deduceISAFamily()` plus a bare `ISAFamily` enum. Upstream
since folded both into a `TargetFeatures` class at
third_party/amd/{include,lib}/Dialect/TritonAMDGPU/IR/TargetFeatures.{h,cpp}:
`getISAFamily()` is now a method that parses the gfx number directly (no
LLVM target-parser dependency), and `getWarpSize()` is a method on the same
class rather than a call site in TargetInfo.cpp. The fix is unchanged in
substance: gfx8xx has no branch in the family switch, so it falls through to
Unknown, and gfx8xx is wave64 the same way every CDNA family here is.

WHAT
----
1. TargetFeatures.h: adds `GCN3` to the `ISAFamily` enum.
2. TargetFeatures.cpp: `getISAFamily()` maps every `gfx8xx` arch (major == 8)
   to `GCN3` -- Polaris and its siblings share one feature set, the same way
   the CDNA and RDNA blocks below group their own generations.
3. TargetFeatures.cpp: `getWarpSize()` returns 64 for `GCN3` (wave64).
   Without this the default 32 is used and kernels run half-dead.

`isCDNA()`/`isRDNA()` already default to false for any family their own
switches do not name, so GCN3 needs no entry there, and `supportDppBroadcast()`
is handled by the sibling gfx803-dpp-broadcast-warpreduce.patch, applied after
this one (its context assumes `ISAFamily::GCN3` already exists).

